From 554803d1fb3356faaa15b4a96211ec11c0405d39 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: austin62jake <340374338+austin62jake@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 8 Nov 2026 04:19:53 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] fix(motion,app): a turning pass that ends inside a longer bar
 leaves its cut at feed

Each profile ride ends at its window's top with a radial move out. When
the bar runs on past that end - a bar longer than the part, or a window
that stops partway along it - the nose sits inside the bar's uncut end,
and that move was a rapid through stock: the meridian law flagged one
RapidInStock per rung and the post was refused.

- StockEnv carries the bar's far end (s_top), read from the stock in
  the part's frame (turning_stock::read).
- StockEnv::runs_past says when the bar goes on past a ride's end.
- prof::ride takes an Exit: Rapid as before, or Feed at the plunge feed
  when the bar runs past. Profile rough and finish choose it from the
  stock; the contour kinds, which read no stock, keep Rapid.
- A bar that ends with the part keeps the exact old path.

Fixes #229

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
